# SAC FROM c0 WITH THE PRIVILEGED CRITIC, AND THE GOAL KEPT FIXED WHEN THE CAR DRIVES THROUGH IT
# (user 2026-11-14: "ok", after the finding below).
# = slurm/local_frl_c0actor_privcritic_t01_ar2.env (lane cost 0.5, the run that did not collapse) with ONLY:
#   GOAL_KEEP_ON_PASS=1 in TRAINING, as scoring and recording have had since 2026-11-02.
# WHY: without it, a pass through the arrival radius above GOAL_ARRIVAL_MAX_SPEED made the environment draw
# a NEW goal (train_env_config_v4_image_goal: core.resample_goal()) and the episode went on, so
#   - a drive-through cost nothing: the car got further goals until it passed one slowly, and that counted
#     as "reached" (the 0.5-cost run logged 3,220 passes over 685 episodes);
#   - the goal image is latched at reset, so the +100 was paid at a place the policy was not shown;
#   - training goal success (0.93 at 40,000 decisions) was not comparable with the score: the same weights
#     with the SAME sampled actions and the goal fixed reach 14/40 in Town01, 8/40 deterministic.
# With it, a drive-through leaves the goal where it is and the episode runs to a fault or the clock, exactly
# as in slurm/il_eval_val.env. Every other setting is the parent's.
. "$REPO/slurm/local_frl_c0actor_privcritic_t01_ar2.env"
export GOAL_KEEP_ON_PASS=1
